# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and its artifacts run on Linux. Without this file
# git checks scripts out with CRLF, and a shell script whose shebang ends in \r fails with
# "no such file or directory" -- naming a file that plainly exists. That cost a container
# start here, and it would have cost a deploy.
#
# `* text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository; the entries below force LF in the working
# tree too, for the files whose interpreter reads the first line literally.
* text=auto

*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.toml        text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to translate anything inside them.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.onnx  binary
*.npz   binary
